    "result_text": "All tests pass and the build succeeds. Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented address normalization applied whenever an owner is created, following the existing `TelephoneNormalizer`/`HouseholdNormalizer` pattern in the codebase.\n\n### New file\n- **`AddressNormalizer.java`** \u2014 canonicalizes a raw address by trimming, collapsing internal whitespace to a single space, upper-casing, then expanding the whole-word abbreviations `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`. Returns `\"\"` for `null` or blank input.\n\n### Wiring in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`\n- The submitted address is normalized on the DTO **before** `validateRequiredFields` runs. This makes a single change propagate correctly to every consumer:\n  - **Required-field check**: it now inspects the normalized value, so an address that is blank only after normalization (e.g. `\"   \"`) is rejected with 400.\n  - **Stored/returned address**: the mapper carries the normalized value into the `Owner`, so `GET` returns `\"12 MAIN STREET\"` etc.\n  - **Household duplicate detection** and the **shared household id**: both read `owner.getAddress()`, which is now the normalized form.\n\nI also updated the `validateRequiredFields` javadoc to note the address is checked in normalized form.\n\n### Tests\n- The 3 new acceptance tests (`coreNormalizesWhitespaceAndCase`, `functionalityExpandsAbbreviations`, `errorRejectsBlankAfterNormalize`) pass.\n- Full suite: **Tests run: 3, Failures: 0, Errors: 0 \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS**.",
